    "title": "100: The confidence ladder: substantiated and vetted tiers, an accept-all workflow, and an audit that rolls a tier back (draft)"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 1919,
      "end_line": 21,
      "line": 21,
      "start": 1347
    },
    "text": "The operator's aim (2026-11-10): **no learning is absolute, but a high degree of confidence is the goal.** Research should find more, keep what it finds, and say how well each claim is supported. As the knowledge base grows with accepted facts, that knowledge helps judge new learnings without expanding trust. Neither a human nor an agent is likely to do better than five independent sources with two trusted ones, so the strongest tier should be cheap for the operator to accept in bulk, and the operator should be able to find out afterwards whether that was a mistake."
  }
